 add('Reproducibility','Existing `.venv` reused: Python 3.10.8, NumPy 2.2.6, SciPy 1.15.3, statsmodels 0.14.5. No package installation. Original inputs and historical artifacts are protected by the new preservation manifest; the initial ladder has its own preservation receipt. A reference-wrapper preflight correction removed an unnecessary scale/unscale round trip so original start arrays replay exactly; a test-only comment-matching correction was recorded before retries. Neither altered the likelihood, samples or numerical gates.\n\nWorkflow: `stage3jr_common.py` (protect/reconstruct), `stage3jr_diagnose.py` (R0 audit), `stage3jr_validation.py`, `stage3jr_freeze.py`, preflight tests, initial `stage3jr_run.py retry`; preserve that trial, freeze `stage3jr_amend.py`, repeat tests and `retry`; then `full`, `reproduce`, `decision`, `summary`, report and final verification. Frozen retry/full commands are not silent rerun commands; existing artifacts should be verified instead. The exact receipts/logs and code snapshots record both numerical versions. Final report path: `docs/stage3jr_beta_binomial_numerical_remediation.md`. Nothing was committed or pushed.')
 add('Remaining limitations','Numerical convergence does not establish a correct scientific mean model, causal identification, solved opportunity generation, absence of selection, or generalization to all NBA players. The historical attempt-volume misfit and measured-player selection remain. Residual wingspan is time invariant; J2 remains a between-player association with repeated outcomes and fixed reference geometry. The bootstrap conditions on the observed measurement and eligibility process. Three-start agreement and positive local information support numerical consistency, not a proof of a globally unique maximum. **No causal claim is made.**')
